  "question": {
    "text": "The number of different ways in which the first twelve natural numbers can be divided into three groups, each having four elements, such that the numbers in each group are in arithmetic progression is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>No group can have a common difference <math><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math> as there is no number <math><mo>≥</mo><mn>13</mn></math><br />If the group containing <math><mn>1</mn></math> has the common difference&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> i.e. if one group is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, there will be two ways to group others - <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7,8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9,10,11,12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9,11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6,8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10,12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>If the group containing <math><mn>1</mn></math> has the common difference&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> i.e. one group is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5,7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, there will be one way to group others <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6,8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9,10,11,12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>If the group containing <math><mn>1</mn></math> has common difference&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> i.e. if one group is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7,10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> there will be one way to group others <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi></mi></math> The number of ways <math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
}